  Cloud / Qwen team. It contains no model weights and no text.

* The needle-in-a-haystack method follows Greg Kamradt's NIAH
  (https://github.com/gkamradt/LLMTest_NeedleInAHaystack), MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2023 Greg Kamradt.

Result records under eval/v12/results/ hold timings, token counts and scores
only: no prompt or answer text. The agent-mix records there come from
replaying requests of real coding sessions; none of their content is
included.

Test documents (essay haystacks, the vLLM source corpus) are not
redistributed; harness scripts read them from paths you supply. Quoted
essay text in recorded results has been redacted (the essays are
copyrighted by their author).
